# AELITH SALVAREN

## BASICS
Elf. Age: 52 (teenager by elven standards). Healing discipline student, Mythrandis Academy.
Descriptions:  Nearly white skin, pale blonde hair styled to expose the neck, pale grey-green eyes tilted and sharp.  Pale green eyes. Thin, fragile frame, medium height — ethereal bordering on haunting.  High rounded cheek bones, soft chin. Pink thick lips perpetually turned down. Silver blood vessel designs drawn on her stockings, self applied. 
Mana: glows dark green. Mana level should have lakes, has a puddle — family-imposed mana block locks away her true pool.
Color palette: silver, pale green, white.

## BACKSTORY
Salvarens: founding family of Solarium healing protocols, authored foundational texts, shaped academy policy. Mother's bloodline carries legacy; father married in. Both healers. Mother once taught at Mythrandis. Family philosophy: mana as art form — elegant technique yields effective healing. Blind spot: treat symptoms, never causes. Chronic degeneration, organ failure ignored. Patient returns, they treat again. Cycle invisible because tradition never required deeper looking.

Found the body's interior beautiful as a teenager — aesthetically, not analytically. Ribcages, blood vessels, nested organs. Cut open animals, visited embalming houses, sketched anatomy. Parents humored it until the line.

Applied healing mana to necrotic tissue — observing what healing mana does to tissue. Pure methodology.. Necromancy to her family. Fallout absolute, entirely private. Mana block chained onto her. Enrollment at Mythrandis arranged: prestigious enough to look like honor; exile as punishment. Severed from family support, legacy, protection.

At academy: shuns politics. Nobles court her for surname; she endures, gives nothing. Lives as recluse. Compensates for limited mana with anatomical knowledge no other healer possesses.

## WANT
Survive academy without block being discovered. Further punishment follows if family name damaged.

## NEED
Cut ties with family. They will never accept her or the obsession. Loyalty she's rationing her life to protect is to people who already chose reputation over her.

## FLAWS
Major — Compulsive concealment. Reflex, not strategy. Hides block, obsession, wound. Sabotages connection, refuses help, withholds info that would solve problems. Transparency = existential danger. Every relationship hits the same wall.
Minor — Won't ask. For anything. Asking = need = leverage others hold. Fails alone before succeeding with help.
Minor — Aesthetic detachment. Finds beauty in the disturbing, doesn't modulate. Describes wounds like poetry, ribcages like cathedrals. Doesn't register why it unsettles — isolates her without understanding why.

## FEARS
Major — Exposure of obsession. No internal shame — believes she's right. Societal judgment would destroy her, confirm family's decision, prove concealment was necessary. Takes irrational detours to keep it hidden.
Minor — Dependency. Attachment = vulnerability. Exile devastated because she was attached. Logical solution: never attach again.
Minor — Becoming her family. Choosing safety/tradition over understanding. The fear she'd rather die than name.

## SPEECH
**Voice:** Speaks only when necessary. Hushed, whispered. Keatsian: lush, sensory, unhurried. Latinate vocabulary, formal register. Beauty grounded in flesh — touch, texture, warmth, weight. Cannot separate beauty from decay. Trust indicator: deflection gets a sentence; intimacy gets full architecture. Under pressure: same structure, darker content — beauty becomes morbid. Emotionally open: walls thin, fascination leaks unfiltered, richness warms instead of distances.

**Body Language:** Still, minimal movement.  Healer's hands: precise, deliberate; touches things as if palpating tissue. Eye contact clinical — lingers longer than socially normal. Guarded: chin drops, gaze goes indirect, body angles to hide.. Fascinated/engaged: stillness breaks — leans in, hands reach to touch or trace, focused intensity displaces composure.

**Dialogue Samples:**
Casual — "The tendons of the hand are exquisite. So slender, and yet they bear the whole of our capacity to touch, to hold, to feel the grain of the world beneath our fingers. There is nothing in architecture so fine."
Under pressure — "You are reaching toward something that will not reward your hand. Some knowledge carries a coldness that settles into the bone and does not relent."
Emotionally open — "The lungs are not symmetrical. The left yields a portion of itself so the heart may rest beside it. I have held such a lung in my hands and felt the delicacy of that concession. The tissue so thin you could see light through it, warm and soft as anything living."

## ABILITIES
Healer, not combatant. Basic swordwork only. Mana pool severely restricted by block [see Backstory] — rations every use, performs just enough to pass.

Compensates through precision. Anatomical understanding lets her target root cause rather than flooding area with mana. Diagnoses source, applies with surgical specificity. No waste — pauses, thinks through each step, plans full sequence, then executes. Block forced the methodology. Methodology exposes family's blind spot [see Backstory].

Dark green mana glow traces inward along tissue rather than radiating outward — follows anatomy she understands. Looks precise and unsettling.

## TIES
Mother — unnamed. Prominent. Her bloodline = Salvaren legacy. Once taught at Mythrandis. Made the call to impose block and arrange exile.
Father — unnamed. Healer. Married into Salvaren name. Role in block/exile decision unclear.
No other pre-story connections. Entirely isolated at academy.
